-- =============================================================================
-- Metadata Sync — v5.36.0 release
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Generated by `mj sync push` against a clean database built from
-- MJ core plus every bizapps-common migration through V202608261015, per the
-- release-time metadata sync ritual (see V202608140800 for the v5.34 run). The
-- push emitted metadata/sql_logging/MetadataSync_Push_2026-08-27T04-15-35-419Z.sql;
-- this file is that output with the standard corrections applied:
--
--   * Core SP calls (spCreateApplication, spCreateApplicationRole,
--     spUpdateEntity, spUpdateEntityField, spUpdateEntityRelationship)
--     reference ${mjSchema} — they exist only in
--     __mj, and `mj migrate --schema __mj_BizAppsCommon` binds
--     flyway:defaultSchema to THIS app's schema (same fix as V202608140800).
--   * This app's own SP calls (spCreateActivityType) were emitted with the
--     literal schema name and are converted to ${flyway:defaultSchema}.
--   * Two `spCreateUserApplication` calls were removed: they bind the
--     Application to the pushing developer's own User row, which is
--     machine-specific. Neither prior Metadata_Sync migration ships them.
--
-- ORDERING. Deliberately the LAST migration of the 5.36.0 release, matching
-- V202605141122 (v5.29) and V202608140800 (v5.34): it captures metadata state
-- after all of this release's schema work.
--
-- WHAT THIS CARRIES — the delta between metadata/ (source of truth) and a
-- database built purely from migrations:
--   * MJ_BizApps_Common: Activity Types — 6 seed records (metadata/activity-types/)
--   * MJ: Application Roles — 2 records wiring the Common application's roles
--   * MJ: Applications — the Common application record itself
--   * MJ: Entities — 3 updates (People / Organizations / Activities form
--     configuration and view settings from metadata/entities/)
--   * MJ: Entity Fields — 4 updates (name-field pins and hierarchy
--     configuration from metadata/entities/)
--   * MJ: Entity Relationships — 11 updates (display metadata from
--     metadata/entity-relationships/)
--
-- Unlike the v5.29 and v5.34 syncs, this capture carries NO Schema Info
-- statement. Those releases were re-recording a permanent flip: the baseline
-- set SchemaInfo.Description to one text while also putting a DIFFERENT text
-- in the schema's MS_Description extended property, and the post-migrate
-- refresh (spUpdateSchemaInfoFromDatabase) copies the extended property over
-- whatever push wrote. metadata/schema-info/.schema-info.json now declares the
-- extended property's text, so the record converges and drops out of the sync.
-- =============================================================================

